From da576b31ab57ec4a65c832e4ae245a008aefad40 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: barracuda156 <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 11:52:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] gyp: link against an external prebuilt V8 with
 --without-bundled-v8

node 26 carries the configure flag: node_use_bundled_v8=false removes
the dependencies on tools/v8_gypfiles/v8.gyp, so torque, mksnapshot
and all of V8 compilation drop out of the gyp build.  New since node
24, upstream also conditions the Darwin force_load of
v8_base_without_compiler in the node executable and the
tools/v8_gypfiles/abseil.gyp dependencies of libnode and cctest on
node_use_bundled_v8, and configure probes pkg-config for a v8.pc (the
v8-14.6 port installs none; the probe is a no-op).  What upstream still
does not wire up is where the V8 symbols then come from.

Add an else-branch in node.gypi supplying the static archives installed
by the v8-14.6 port (every linkable target - node, node_mksnapshot,
cctest, embedtest - includes node.gypi, so one patch point covers all),
and give the force_load in the node executable - required so the node
binary re-exports the full V8 API to native addons - an else-branch
pointing at the installed archive.

The else-branch also supplies include dirs: deps/v8/include, which the
dropped v8.gyp dependencies used to propagate through
direct_dependent_settings (at node 26 every includer lists it itself;
kept so the branch stays self-sufficient), and
deps/v8/third_party/abseil-cpp for node's own absl use
(absl::SetMutexDeadlockDetectionMode in src/node.cc): with abseil.gyp
out of the graph nothing else puts the absl headers on the include
path, and the code comes from libv8_absl.a.  The abseil source patches
that follow keep those headers identical to the ones the v8 port
compiled its archives from.  (nodejs24 needed a patch of its own to
gate abseil.gyp; node 26 has that upstream, so only the include dir
remains and lives here.)

Archives, as installed by the v8-14.6 port: libv8_initializers.a is
not optional - the harness builds the CSA/Turboshaft builtin
generators once, there, instead of a second time into v8_base.
libv8_absl.a is the abseil dependency closure of v8_libbase, merged by
the Portfile from the constituent absl archives so that single-pass
ld64 archive resolution needs no topological ordering among them.
Maglev, new at 14.6 and built by the v8 port's maglev variant, lives
inside libv8_base_without_compiler.a, so the list is the same nine as
at 13.6.  V8 links highway (json-stringifier) and simdutf; the v8 port
uses the system libraries from ports highway and simdutf, so the
archives' link interface needs -lhwy (added here) and -lsimdutf (which
--shared-simdutf puts on every link line, with the -L for both).

The @V8_LIBDIR@ placeholder is substituted by the Portfile.  Compile-
time headers stay the in-tree deps/v8/include, which the next patch
brings to parity with the port's installed headers (the 14.6 series
patches three public headers).  The libnode (node_shared) target has
the same bundled-only force_load condition and is left alone: this
port does not build the shared library.
---
 node.gyp  | 11 +++++++++++
 node.gypi | 46 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 57 insertions(+)

diff --git a/node.gyp b/node.gyp
index 1373c89..eebc032 100644
--- a/node.gyp
+++ b/node.gyp
@@ -668,12 +668,23 @@
             },
           },
           'conditions': [
+            # v8_base_without_compiler must be force-loaded in full: it is
+            # what re-exports the whole V8 API from the node binary so that
+            # native addons can resolve V8 symbols at runtime.  With
+            # --without-bundled-v8 the archive lives in the v8 port's prefix
+            # (@V8_LIBDIR@, substituted by the Portfile), not in PRODUCT_DIR.
             ['node_use_bundled_v8=="true"', {
               'xcode_settings': {
                 'OTHER_LDFLAGS': [
                   '-Wl,-force_load,<(PRODUCT_DIR)/<(STATIC_LIB_PREFIX)v8_base_without_compiler<(STATIC_LIB_SUFFIX)',
                 ],
               },
+            }, {
+              'xcode_settings': {
+                'OTHER_LDFLAGS': [
+                  '-Wl,-force_load,@V8_LIBDIR@/libv8_base_without_compiler.a',
+                ],
+              },
             }],
             ['node_use_bundled_v8=="true" and OS != "aix" and OS != "os400" and OS != "mac" and OS != "ios"', {
               'ldflags': [
diff --git a/node.gypi b/node.gypi
index 9eb972a..93859fb 100644
--- a/node.gypi
+++ b/node.gypi
@@ -107,6 +107,52 @@
         'tools/v8_gypfiles/v8.gyp:v8_snapshot',
         'tools/v8_gypfiles/v8.gyp:v8_libplatform',
       ],
+    }, {
+      # --without-bundled-v8: supply what the dropped v8.gyp and abseil.gyp
+      # dependencies used to provide.  Headers first.  deps/v8/include is
+      # what v8.gyp propagated through direct_dependent_settings (at node
+      # 26 every includer lists it itself; kept so this branch stays
+      # self-sufficient - duplicates are harmless to gyp).
+      'include_dirs': [
+        'deps/v8/include',
+        # abseil headers for node's own absl use (src/node.cc).  The code
+        # comes from libv8_absl.a below, so tools/v8_gypfiles/abseil.gyp is
+        # not built in this configuration (node.gyp gates it on
+        # node_use_bundled_v8).  Header/archive parity: the port's absl
+        # patches keep these headers identical to the ones the v8 port
+        # compiled the archives from.
+        'deps/v8/third_party/abseil-cpp',
+      ],
+      # Then the archives installed by the v8 port.  Absolute paths, not
+      # -L/-l: on Darwin -l would also match dylibs, and ld64 resolves
+      # archive members regardless of command line order, so no grouping
+      # is needed.  @V8_LIBDIR@ is substituted by the Portfile.
+      # link_settings on a static_library propagates to the executables
+      # that link it.  libv8_initializers.a carries the CSA/Turboshaft
+      # builtin generators (built once there by the harness, not a second
+      # time into v8_base).  libv8_absl.a is the abseil dependency closure
+      # of v8_libbase, merged from the individual absl archives by the
+      # Portfile (single archive, so no inter-archive ordering).  Maglev
+      # (14.6) lives inside v8_base_without_compiler.
+      'link_settings': {
+        'libraries': [
+          '@V8_LIBDIR@/libv8_libplatform.a',
+          '@V8_LIBDIR@/libv8_base_without_compiler.a',
+          '@V8_LIBDIR@/libv8_compiler.a',
+          '@V8_LIBDIR@/libv8_initializers.a',
+          '@V8_LIBDIR@/libv8_snapshot.a',
+          '@V8_LIBDIR@/libv8_torque_generated.a',
+          '@V8_LIBDIR@/libv8_libsampler.a',
+          '@V8_LIBDIR@/libv8_libbase.a',
+          '@V8_LIBDIR@/libv8_absl.a',
+          # V8 links highway (json-stringifier); the v8 port uses the
+          # system libhwy from port highway rather than the vendored copy.
+          # -L${prefix}/lib is on every link line already through
+          # --shared-simdutf-libpath, which also resolves the archives'
+          # simdutf references.
+          '-lhwy',
+        ],
+      },
     }],
     [ 'node_use_v8_platform=="true"', {
       'defines': [
-- 
2.43.0

